exports[`a medallion project on databricks > says in its passport what each check does, where results are, and what is cleansed 1`] = `
"## Quality

### customers

#### \`dev.bronze.customers\`

Checked by Databricks on each pipeline update. Results: the pipeline's event log, published as a table.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`email_not_null\`: \`email\` has a value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`email_min_length\`: \`email\` has at least 3 characters; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`email_pattern\`: \`email\` matches \`^[^@]+@[^@]+$\`; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`name_max_length\`: \`name\` has at most 100 characters; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`country_invalidvalues\`: \`country\` is one of \`GB\`, \`IE\` or \`FR\`, or has no value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`status_missingvalues\`: \`status\` has a value and is not \`n/a\`; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`age_minimum\`: \`age\` is at least 0; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`age_exclusive_maximum\`: \`age\` is less than 150; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`score_multiple_of\`: \`score\` is a multiple of 5; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`tags_min_items\`: \`tags\` has at least 1 item; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`tags_max_items\`: \`tags\` has at most 5 items; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`tags_unique_items\`: \`tags\` has items that are all different; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`some_customers\`: Not enforced: it counts all rows, which is checked only when the platform turns on checks.
- \`one_per_person\`: Each person is one customer. Not checked: it is written for people to follow.

Cleansing:

- Nothing is cleansed.
- Its timestamps are in Europe/London.

#### \`dev.silver.customers_clean\`

Checked by Databricks on each pipeline update. Results: the pipeline's event log, published as a table.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`dev.silver.customers_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`email_not_null\`: \`email\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`dev.silver.customers_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`dev.silver.customers_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`email_min_length\`: \`email\` has at least 3 characters; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`email_pattern\`: \`email\` matches \`^[^@]+@[^@]+$\`; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`name_max_length\`: \`name\` has at most 100 characters; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`country_invalidvalues\`: \`country\` is one of \`GB\`, \`IE\` or \`FR\`, or has no value; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`status_missingvalues\`: \`status\` has a value and is not \`n/a\`; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`age_minimum\`: \`age\` is at least 0; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`age_exclusive_maximum\`: \`age\` is less than 150; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`score_multiple_of\`: \`score\` is a multiple of 5; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`tags_min_items\`: \`tags\` has at least 1 item; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`tags_max_items\`: \`tags\` has at most 5 items; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`tags_unique_items\`: \`tags\` has items that are all different; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`recent\`: \`updated_at >= TIMESTAMP '2000-01-01'\`; a row that fails stops the update.
- \`some_customers\`: Not enforced: it counts all rows, which is checked only when the platform turns on checks.
- \`one_per_person\`: Each person is one customer. Not checked: it is written for people to follow.

Cleansing:

- \`email\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; lower case.
- \`name\`: empty text becomes no value.
- \`country\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; \`United Kingdom\` becomes \`GB\`, \`UK\` becomes \`GB\`, \`-\` becomes no value; upper case.
- \`status\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; no value becomes \`active\`.
- \`vip\`: no value becomes false.
- \`contacted_at\`: converted from UTC to Europe/London.
- \`last_seen\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- \`updated_at\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- One row for each \`id\`: the last by \`updated_at\`.
- Its timestamps are not all in one time zone: see each column above.

### orders

#### \`dev.bronze.orders\`

Checked by Databricks on each pipeline update. Results: the pipeline's event log, published as a table.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`customer_id_not_null\`: \`customer_id\` has a value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; counted only: bronze keeps raw rows.

Cleansing:

- Nothing is cleansed.
- Its timestamps are in Europe/London.

#### \`dev.silver.orders_clean\`

Checked by Databricks on each pipeline update. Results: the pipeline's event log, published as a table.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`dev.silver.orders_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`customer_id_not_null\`: \`customer_id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`dev.silver.orders_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`dev.silver.orders_clean_quarantine\`.

Cleansing:

- \`status\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; upper case.
- \`updated_at\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- One row for each \`id\`: the last by \`updated_at\`.
- Its timestamps are in UTC.
"
`;

