"## Quality

### customers

#### \`crm.bronze.customers\`

None of these checks runs here.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`email_not_null\`: \`email\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`email_min_length\`: \`email\` has at least 3 characters. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`email_pattern\`: \`email\` matches \`^[^@]+@[^@]+$\`. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`name_max_length\`: \`name\` has at most 100 characters. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`country_invalidvalues\`: \`country\` is one of \`GB\`, \`IE\` or \`FR\`, or has no value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`status_missingvalues\`: \`status\` has a value and is not \`n/a\`. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`age_minimum\`: \`age\` is at least 0. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`age_exclusive_maximum\`: \`age\` is less than 150. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`score_multiple_of\`: \`score\` is a multiple of 5. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`tags_min_items\`: \`tags\` has at least 1 item. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`tags_max_items\`: \`tags\` has at most 5 items. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`tags_unique_items\`: \`tags\` has items that are all different. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`some_customers\`: the number of rows is more than 0. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`one_per_person\`: Each person is one customer. Not checked: it is written for people to follow.

Cleansing:

- Nothing is cleansed.
- Its timestamps are in Europe/London.

#### \`crm.silver.customers_clean\`

Checked by DuckDB each time \`run.sql\` runs. Results: the run prints each check's failing rows (in Azure, in the job's log), and keeps them in \`silver._ingestron_checks\` in the run's database (in Azure, only for that run).

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`crm.silver.customers_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`email_not_null\`: \`email\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`crm.silver.customers_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`crm.silver.customers_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`email_min_length\`: \`email\` has at least 3 characters; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`email_pattern\`: \`email\` matches \`^[^@]+@[^@]+$\`; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`name_max_length\`: \`name\` has at most 100 characters; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`country_invalidvalues\`: \`country\` is one of \`GB\`, \`IE\` or \`FR\`, or has no value; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`status_missingvalues\`: \`status\` has a value and is not \`n/a\`; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`age_minimum\`: \`age\` is at least 0; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`age_exclusive_maximum\`: \`age\` is less than 150; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`score_multiple_of\`: \`score\` is a multiple of 5; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`tags_min_items\`: \`tags\` has at least 1 item; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`tags_max_items\`: \`tags\` has at most 5 items; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`tags_unique_items\`: \`tags\` has items that are all different; a row that fails is kept, and counted.
- \`recent\`: \`updated_at >= TIMESTAMP '2000-01-01'\`; a row that fails stops the run, and nothing is published.
- \`some_customers\`: the number of rows is more than 0, counted after the table is built, in the same run; if it fails, the run goes on.
- \`one_per_person\`: Each person is one customer. Not checked: it is written for people to follow.

Cleansing:

- \`email\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; lower case.
- \`name\`: empty text becomes no value.
- \`country\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; \`United Kingdom\` becomes \`GB\`, \`UK\` becomes \`GB\`, \`-\` becomes no value; upper case.
- \`status\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; no value becomes \`active\`.
- \`vip\`: no value becomes false.
- \`contacted_at\`: converted from UTC to Europe/London.
- \`last_seen\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- \`updated_at\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- One row for each \`id\`: the last by \`updated_at\`.
- Its timestamps are not all in one time zone: see each column above.

### orders

#### \`crm.bronze.orders\`

None of these checks runs here.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`customer_id_not_null\`: \`customer_id\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.

Cleansing:

- Nothing is cleansed.
- Its timestamps are in Europe/London.

#### \`crm.silver.orders_clean\`

Checked by DuckDB each time \`run.sql\` runs. Results: the run prints each check's failing rows (in Azure, in the job's log), and keeps them in \`silver._ingestron_checks\` in the run's database (in Azure, only for that run).

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`crm.silver.orders_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`customer_id_not_null\`: \`customer_id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`crm.silver.orders_clean_quarantine\`.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the table, and kept in \`crm.silver.orders_clean_quarantine\`.

Cleansing:

- \`status\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; upper case.
- \`updated_at\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- One row for each \`id\`: the last by \`updated_at\`.
- Its timestamps are in UTC.
