exports[`a medallion project on synapse > says in its passport what each check does, where results are, and what is cleansed 1`] = `
"## Quality

### customers

#### \`crm_dev.bronze.customers\`

None of these checks runs here.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`email_not_null\`: \`email\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`email_min_length\`: \`email\` has at least 3 characters. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`email_pattern\`: \`email\` matches \`^[^@]+@[^@]+$\`. Not enforced: serverless T-SQL has no regular expressions.
- \`name_max_length\`: \`name\` has at most 100 characters. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`country_invalidvalues\`: \`country\` is one of \`GB\`, \`IE\` or \`FR\`, or has no value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`status_missingvalues\`: \`status\` has a value and is not \`n/a\`. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`age_minimum\`: \`age\` is at least 0. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`age_exclusive_maximum\`: \`age\` is less than 150. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`score_multiple_of\`: \`score\` is a multiple of 5. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`tags_min_items\`: \`tags\` has at least 1 item. Not enforced: views type no arrays.
- \`tags_max_items\`: \`tags\` has at most 5 items. Not enforced: views type no arrays.
- \`tags_unique_items\`: \`tags\` has items that are all different. Not enforced: views type no arrays.
- \`some_customers\`: the number of rows is more than 0. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`one_per_person\`: Each person is one customer. Not checked: it is written for people to follow.

Cleansing:

- Nothing is cleansed.
- Its timestamps are in Europe/London.

#### \`crm_dev.silver.customers_clean\`

Checked by Synapse serverless SQL: the view leaves out the rows a \`drop\` check fails each time it is queried, and \`checks.sql\` counts every check when it runs. Results: what \`checks.sql\` returns; nothing keeps them.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`email_not_null\`: \`email\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`email_min_length\`: \`email\` has at least 3 characters; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`email_pattern\`: \`email\` matches \`^[^@]+@[^@]+$\`. Not enforced: serverless T-SQL has no regular expressions.
- \`name_max_length\`: \`name\` has at most 100 characters; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`country_invalidvalues\`: \`country\` is one of \`GB\`, \`IE\` or \`FR\`, or has no value; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`status_missingvalues\`: \`status\` has a value and is not \`n/a\`; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`age_minimum\`: \`age\` is at least 0; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`age_exclusive_maximum\`: \`age\` is less than 150; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`score_multiple_of\`: \`score\` is a multiple of 5; a row that fails stays in the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`tags_min_items\`: \`tags\` has at least 1 item. Not enforced: views type no arrays.
- \`tags_max_items\`: \`tags\` has at most 5 items. Not enforced: views type no arrays.
- \`tags_unique_items\`: \`tags\` has items that are all different. Not enforced: views type no arrays.
- \`recent\`: \`[updated_at] >= '2000-01-01'\`. Not enforced: a view can't stop a load; checks.sql checks this rule and raises an error when it runs.
- \`some_customers\`: the number of rows is more than 0, counted by \`checks.sql\`, over the rows the view keeps; if it fails, \`checks.sql\` returns the count.
- \`one_per_person\`: Each person is one customer. Not checked: it is written for people to follow.
- Keeping the rows a \`drop\` check leaves out. Not enforced: a view keeps no rows to quarantine; checks.sql returns how many rows each drop check leaves out instead.
- Keeping the checks' results. Not enforced: a view keeps no results; checks.sql returns each check's counts instead when it runs.

Cleansing:

- \`email\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; lower case.
- \`name\`: empty text becomes no value.
- \`country\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; \`United Kingdom\` becomes \`GB\`, \`UK\` becomes \`GB\`, \`-\` becomes no value; upper case.
- \`status\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; no value becomes \`active\`.
- \`vip\`: no value becomes false.
- \`contacted_at\`: converted from UTC to Europe/London.
- \`last_seen\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- \`updated_at\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- One row for each \`id\`: the last by \`updated_at\`.
- Its timestamps are not all in one time zone: see each column above.

### orders

#### \`crm_dev.bronze.orders\`

None of these checks runs here.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`customer_id_not_null\`: \`customer_id\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value. Not enforced: it is applied only in a layer whose does lists check.

Cleansing:

- Nothing is cleansed.
- Its timestamps are in Europe/London.

#### \`crm_dev.silver.orders_clean\`

Checked by Synapse serverless SQL: the view leaves out the rows a \`drop\` check fails each time it is queried, and \`checks.sql\` counts every check when it runs. Results: what \`checks.sql\` returns; nothing keeps them.

- \`id_not_null\`: \`id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`customer_id_not_null\`: \`customer_id\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- \`updated_at_not_null\`: \`updated_at\` has a value; a row that fails is left out of the view, and \`checks.sql\` counts it.
- Keeping the rows a \`drop\` check leaves out. Not enforced: a view keeps no rows to quarantine; checks.sql returns how many rows each drop check leaves out instead.
- Keeping the checks' results. Not enforced: a view keeps no results; checks.sql returns each check's counts instead when it runs.

Cleansing:

- \`status\`: spaces at either end removed; empty text becomes no value; upper case.
- \`updated_at\`: converted from Europe/London to UTC.
- One row for each \`id\`: the last by \`updated_at\`.
- Its timestamps are in UTC.
"
`;

